		text: "Corresponding dates, availability filters, range limits, cell templates and quick selections. Import DateCellTemplateDirective in the template owner. The context provides date/$implicit, calendar, secondaryDate (nullable), secondaryCalendar, selected, disabled and today. Months are one-based. The library retains its button, date name, focus and restrictions; custom text becomes an accessible description. Do not nest interactive controls. Templates replace default contents, so render secondaryDate explicitly if desired. Verify content sizing and contrast. import { Component } from '@angular/core';\nimport { NgxNepaliDualpicker, DateCellTemplateDirective } from 'ngx-nepali-dualpicker';\n@Component({\n  standalone: true, imports: [NgxNepaliDualpicker, DateCellTemplateDirective],\n  template: `<ngx-nepali-dualpicker [config]=\"{ calendar: 'BS', inline: true }\">\n    <ng-template ndpDateCell let-date let-disabled=\"disabled\" let-secondary=\"secondaryDate\">\n      <span>{{ date.day }}</span><small>{{ disabled ? 'Unavailable' : 'Rs 500' }}</small>\n      @if (secondary) { <small>AD {{ secondary.month }}/{{ secondary.day }}</small> }\n    </ng-template>\n  </ngx-nepali-dualpicker>`,\n})\nexport class BookingCalendar {}",
